eos-2016.05" change_id="I33d51d4ef09b218c14173d39a12795f0cef6bb40" commit="53321fc8c95b108e5f4e1182b9ffdff548398ba2" commit_message="gru: Change UART _Static_assert() condition to preprocessor #if  _Static_assert() gets evaluated even when the code path it's in is unreachable (e.g. inside an if (0) block). Unfortunately, Kconfigs that depend on a disabled Kconfig are always 0, meaning that CONFIG_CONSOLE_SERIAL_UART_ADDRESS on Gru cannot evaluate to UART2 when CONFIG_CONSOLE_SERIAL (which it depends on) is disabled. Switch the condition it is wrapped in to a preprocessor #if so that the _Static_assert() is not evaluated when building without serial support.  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=Built and booted Kevin without serial  Change-Id: I33d51d4ef09b218c14173d39a12795f0cef6bb40 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361581 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361581" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/81/361581/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6293887f7123c6885d0f396b33da9166d7c230c5" commit="a96ffc8cacebd104352222897c974645f6878eb7" commit_message="coreboot/libpayload: Clean up configs for Gru and Kevin  This patch removes some redundant or incorrect Kconfig options from Gru and Kevin config files which are already part of the defaults anyway. Also add the OHCI host controller driver to Gru because its depthcharge code is actually trying to use that. Alphabetized Kevin's coreboot config to put it in line with Gru.  Added the deselection line for CONFIG_CONSOLE_SERIAL to both boards to make our build system (with the fwserial addition for developer but not production builds) work, because otherwise the serial console is by default enabled in all images.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:361581 BUG=None TEST=Built Kevin image.bin, confirmed that it booted and had no serial output.  Change-Id: I6293887f7123c6885d0f396b33da9166d7c230c5 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361571 Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="361571" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/71/361571/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic8692a3a70b6ca90732e37fe72bf4137c8c9b7a2" commit="cace42c87c97fc770179331626c69de9eaba5b0a" commit_message="Enable branch PFQ to also rev Android  BUG=b:27441351 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic8692a3a70b6ca90732e37fe72bf4137c8c9b7a2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361791 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David Riley &lt;davidriley@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="361791" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/91/361791/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I3c09a183d0a3c652d5141f0569246f67c2fea23d" commit="d5dcc054ffaad8f531122c50e2e276e6d0119636" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm: add implicit in-fences to atomic  This change adds GPU-display sync in DRM atomic layer for dma-bufs shared between display driver and GPU. DRM atomic layer will collect all reservation objects and fences from framebuffers in atomic state, merge them into single fence array and assign to plane states so kernel will wait for these fences before 